keywords:
  - large language models
  - model-as-a-service
  - service-level monitoring
  - API brokerage
  - behavioral consistency
  - energy statistics
abstract: >-
  Aggregated large language model services expose declared model identifiers while hiding the backend
  configurations fulfilling client requests. We present HuePrint, a black-box framework that audits brokered
  endpoint consistency via structured color elicitation and continuous geometric distribution comparison without
  model weights or token probabilities. Across 38,688 cloud responses spanning 56 endpoints and 12 backends, HuePrint
  lowers 30-call-per-side equal error rates over single-word baselines from 4.52-5.23% to 0.94-1.00% on our
  development cohort and from 6.25-8.04% to 3.49-5.00% across 20 locked endpoints, reaching 0.00% at 60-150
  calls/side. In a 20-model parity benchmark, 30-call/side HuePrint averages 5.18% within-family EER across all
  ten balanced splits (0.00-7.89%; matched split 0.00%) at $0.0068 query cost, outperforming open-set LLMmap
  (10.53-34.39% across 1-3 traces) and cost-matched long-form kernels (11.09-19.47%), avoids LLMmap's
  safety-triggering probes, and scores traces over 15,000 times faster locally. Regularized RGB energy halves
  shallow-census error relative to exact-hex divergence (5.36% vs. 10.71%), and a multi-scale hybrid cuts
  cross-provider error from 16.67% to 5.93%. Across 21-day cross-gateway transfers, budget-matched frozen thresholds
  flag 1/14 raw (0/14 self-centered) same-label pairs vs. 6/14 equality-test rejections while catching 182/182 swaps.
  In offline replay, two-stage confirmation cuts false alerts from 14 to 1 across 100 same-label windows and flags
  186/190 within-family substitutions under one cent expected cost.
